## Verdict

PASS. The new `<p data-spending-budget>` sentence renders in reading order
directly under the card `<h5>`, before the headline figure and the
`<details>` expander, as plain text with no new role/aria/hidden
attributes; its classes are byte-identical to existing sibling secondary
text; heading order is unchanged and unbroken end-to-end; contrast clears
AA in both themes by a wide margin (7.63:1 light, 10.18:1 dark); axe-core
reports zero violations against the real built stylesheets in both themes;
the middle dot is a literal U+00B7 character consistent with existing
usage; and all Supporting-details paragraphs remain intact and readable
without the relocated sentence. The attempt-2 Go-only fix (branching on the
rendered strings instead of a separate rounding comparison) does not touch
markup, so none of the attempt-1 a11y findings are disturbed — confirmed
directly by re-rendering and re-auditing at this commit rather than assumed.
